#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# log1p

#% text
# `log1p(x)` gives `log(1 + x)`, computed so that it stays accurate when `x` is small.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For machine reals near 0, `log(1 + x)` loses the digits of `x` when `1 + x` is rounded; `log1p` keeps them.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
log1p(1.0e-12)
#% output
#= 9.999999999995e-13

#% cell
log(1 + 1.0e-12)
#% output
#= 1.000088900581841e-12

#% cell
log1p(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# It inverts `expm1`:

#% cell
log1p(expm1(0.3))
#% output
#= 0.3

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `expm1`
